/**
 * @defgroup permutation_operators Permutation operators
 * @brief Mutation, crossover, neighborhood generation, and perturbation for permutations.
 *
 * @par Representation requirements
 * Operators are parameterized by the representation type, not tied to std::vector.
 * Use a mutable random-access sequence supporting std::begin(), std::end(),
 * std::size(), and operator[], with assignable and swappable elements.
 * Typical representations include std::vector, std::array, and std::deque;
 * contiguous storage is supported but is not required. Representations must
 * satisfy the selected optimizer's copy and independent-storage requirements.
 *
 * @par Input and output requirements
 * Representations must contain at least two elements. Output references must
 * refer to initialized, independent representations of the required size;
 * for example, output vectors must already be resized to match their inputs.
 * Operators need not allocate or resize outputs. Crossover parents and outputs
 * must have matching sizes. Output storage must not alias inputs or other outputs.
 *
 * @par Crossover values
 * Ox and Pmx require both parents to be permutations of the integers in
 * [0, size()), since gene values index internal lookup tables. Swap, insertion,
 * and reversal operators do not impose this integer-encoding requirement.
 *
 * @par Randomness and concurrency
 * RNG must provide the sampling functions used by the selected operator.
 * It must be copy-constructible because cloning an operator copies its stored RNG;
 * the RNG itself does not need a clone() method. Constructors initialize the RNG
 * from an rvalue, using a move constructor if available or a copy constructor
 * otherwise. Default construction is required only when no RNG instance is supplied.
 * Concurrent calls on the same operator require a thread-safe RNG, such as
 * metah::ThreadLocalRandom.
 */

/**
 * @dir src/metah/operators/permut
 * @brief Permutation operators; see @ref permutation_operators for shared requirements.
 */
